{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1792304208,"nonce":"bPfhNJZAvrzlH3RP/HFica6pMpk=","target":"09a92b53f6419228bf3afeb23e9d58924b164fdf27de1dd6f20aa08486088de5","message":"A window with a 3D scene presents in about 110 ms a frame, whatever changed\n\n**What**\n\nMeasured by ChimpMonk (its issue 9f4ae15) on ashui 3d9c201, macOS, Ash 0.1.10, windowed, with ASHUI_FRAME_LOG, one trivial toolbar toggle per frame as the only change:\n\n- no scene loaded: 17 ms a frame (present 14 ms, 360 primitives);\n- any scene loaded: 117 ms a frame (present 109 ms, about 3100 primitives; GPU encode 2 to 4 ms, layout 1 ms), the same for every scene tried (collider-workshop, lost-crate, harbour-3d, flag, rig-ranger, starter). Every hover, transition or node drag redraws the window at about 9 fps.\n- It scales with the window: 1280x800 presents in 109 ms, 800x560 in 76 ms, so roughly 50 ms fixed and 57 ms per logical megapixel.\n\nRuled out by ChimpMonk, each measured: its panels (hiding all changes nothing), its graph canvases, its grid, marks, transparent and selection passes (skipping each leaves 117 ms), -D ashui_scene_stencil, the CPU side (display list 2 to 3 ms), reactive work. Its Scene3D is `new Scene3D(camera, Scene3D.DEFAULT.lighting, 1, background, 1)`: one directional light, no bloom, no effects, no antialiasing.\n\n**Where to look**\n\nThe cost is GPU time that present waits on, and it is there with nothing changed in the scene, so the scene layer looks to be drawn again for every redraw of the window. In haxe/ashui/core/render/ScenePainter.hx:\n\n- Whether an unchanged scene layer is kept as its texture and composited, not drawn again; a window redraw for a hover should cost the UI pass and one blit. The canvases already stop ticking when paused; the scene layer may not have an equivalent.\n- Window-sized targets: the colour target in Rgba16float, depth, and the glow and velocity targets (lines 724 to 728) are made at the layer's size; check whether they are made, cleared or resolved every frame when no effect asks for them.\n- The shadow map (shadowTarget, line 589) is drawn each frame for one directional light, at what size.\n- The image-based lighting inputs: whether the environment's prefiltering happens once.\n- A full-window copy or resolve at the end.\n\n**To do**\n\nA GPU timestamp query around each pass of ScenePainter.render, printed with the frame log, so the 100 ms has a name; or ChimpMonk's pass-by-pass bisect, which it has offered. Then the fix, with a test that a redraw with an unchanged scene draws no scene pass. Expected after: a hover redraw of the editor with a scene costs about what it does without one.\n\n**Also**\n\nChimpMonk measured, for the per-node heap cost (d106687): five panels open held 4703 live Watches (5229 slots) at about 2650 layout nodes, 1.8 Watches a node.","files":null}]}